Kafka Fundamentals - Top 20 Interview Questions (Senior Java Developer / Solution Architect)
1. What is Apache Kafka?

Answer: Apache Kafka is a distributed event streaming platform used for building real-time data pipelines and event-driven applications. It stores data as an immutable log and allows producers to publish events while consumers read them independently.

Interview Discussion:

Distributed system
Event streaming platform
Persistent storage
Horizontal scalability
2. Why Kafka became so popular?

Answer: Kafka provides:

High Throughput
Low Latency
Scalability
Fault Tolerance
Message Replay
Event Streaming

Real-world Example: Banking transaction events flowing between multiple microservices.

